WEBVTT

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:09.090
The view from the peak is amazing.

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:10.130
Yeah.

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:11.740
It is.

00:00:11.930 --> 00:00:13.850
I'm going to take a panorama shot.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:16.510
Slowly

00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:18.150
I made it!

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:20.910
Good effort, Aki-chan.

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:26.250
So who won the race, anyway?

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:27.700
I did.

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:30.500
You're so childish, Nadeshiko-chan.

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:33.380
You could've gone easier on me.

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:37.260
The lion hunts the hare with all its might.

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:41.620
So anyway, Aki-chan, you owe us both drinks.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:44.270
Dang... All right.

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:49.730
Hey, you made it.

00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:52.780
These stairs are tough.

00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:58.920
Those are the Izu Islands you can
vaguely see over the horizon, huh?

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:04.040
That one's Toshima, and that big 
island is apparently Izu Oshima.

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:06.420
Izu Oshima, huh?

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:08.970
I want to try island camping someday, too.

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:10.420
Yeah.

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:13.610
Shima Rin in Shimane, camping on Izu Oshima.

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:15.520
It's a Shima Shima Shima camp trip.

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:17.100
Lame.

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:22.310
Come to think of it, there are plains 
past that mountain over there, too.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:28.450
Apparently there's a legit treehouse there
 that was made by a treehouse designer.

00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:29.690
Wow!

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:32.290
I wanna see the treehouse!

00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:34.320
Yeah! A legit treehouse!

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:38.780
<i>Staaare...</i>

00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:44.120
I don't think we'll have time to go now.

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:46.080
Of course not...

00:01:46.690 --> 00:01:50.200
I knew Izu was huge, but it's super huge.

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:51.840
I know.

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:57.320
Now that I'm sitting still, I'm really cold.

00:01:57.320 --> 00:01:59.590
You should have bundled up 
more before coming up here.

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:01.900
The sun will be setting soon.

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:03.410
Shall we get going?

00:02:03.410 --> 00:02:04.570
Yeah.

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:44.200
<b>(2) Episode 10
Izu Camping!! On the Way</b>

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:44.090
Now we just need to make it to the campsite.

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:46.740
Although it's a pretty long drive.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:51.870
Come to think of it, the only camping-ish 
activity we've done so far is shopping.

00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:57.110
It's all good. Outclub quality 
is all about the chill factor.

00:03:57.110 --> 00:03:59.610
Sensei, what about a hot spring?

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:02.880
Okay, how about we visit on the way?

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:06.880
Could I ask you to look for a hot spring 
that's available for day visits?

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:08.010
Got it.

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:10.410
Let's see...

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:15.020
I never knew Izu had so many hot springs.

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:16.540
You're right.

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:17.900
That's crazy.

00:04:18.210 --> 00:04:21.030
Izu was an underwater volcano long ago.

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:23.310
So it has a lot of hot springs.

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:25.280
Underwater Volcano

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:25.280
Honshu

00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:25.280
20 million years ago

00:04:24.350 --> 00:04:28.410
And a lot of the geospots were 
created by volcanic activity, too.

00:04:28.730 --> 00:04:32.410
Oh, also, I don't want Shima-san 
to get cold after our bath,

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:36.420
so please try to find one 
close to the campsite.

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:41.170
I bet you'd freeze solid riding 
a bike right after a bath.

00:04:42.270 --> 00:04:43.670
<i>Freeze solid...</i>

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:56.190
I'm ice cold.

00:04:56.250 --> 00:05:00.690
<b>Icy Cold</b>

00:04:56.250 --> 00:05:00.690
<b>Shimarin Dango Ice Cream</b>

00:04:56.690 --> 00:04:57.960
<i>New!</i>

00:04:56.710 --> 00:05:00.690
<b>Icy 
Cold</b>

00:04:56.710 --> 00:05:00.690
<b>Shimarin Dango Ice Cream</b>

00:04:56.710 --> 00:05:00.690
<b>New</b>

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:00.690
<i>Icy cold Shimarin Dango Ice Cream.</i>

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:09.540
Nadeshiko-chan, what do 
you think of this one?

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:10.950
Let's see.

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:15.460
"A natural hot spring formed on a pier."

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:20.090
-Feel the scenery of Nishiizu on your skin\h\h\h\hA hidden bath by the beach-

00:05:15.890 --> 00:05:20.090
"Let the sea breeze wash over you 
as you enjoy the Dougashima waters."

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:22.830
Nice! This place is so nice!

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:23.640
Right?

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:25.970
It's not that far from the campsite, either.

00:05:26.350 --> 00:05:29.200
Dougashima Hot Spring is
 just two kilometers away.

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:32.280
We could watch the sun set as we take a dip.

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:34.480
So it's settled, then!

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:38.960
Rin-chan!

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:43.730
We're going to a hot spring called 
Dougashima Hot Spring up ahead.

00:05:46.510 --> 00:05:47.720
Are you all right?

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:49.620
I'll make it.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:52.320
It's not much farther. Hang in there.

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:53.870
Yeah...

00:05:54.370 --> 00:05:57.190
<i>I'm suddenly feeling sleepy.</i>

00:05:57.710 --> 00:05:59.950
<i>I did leave in the middle 
of the night, after all.</i>

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:04.630
<i>No, no.</i>

00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:07.040
<i>We're almost there.</i>

00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:10.800
<i>Two kilometers to the hot spring!</i>

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:16.940
<i>Finally made it.</i>

00:06:16.940 --> 00:06:18.730
Long ride, huh, Rin-chan?

00:06:18.730 --> 00:06:22.140
All right, let's go warm up in the hot spring.

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:24.150
<b>Women</b>

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:30.450
Man, this is the best.

00:06:30.450 --> 00:06:32.910
The sunset is gorgeous.

00:06:33.130 --> 00:06:35.840
Good thing we made it by sundown, huh?

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:37.910
I know. We just barely made it.

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:43.080
We wouldn't have gotten to see this 
if we'd followed our original plan.

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:47.670
It got a little stressful, but we 
made our lemons into lemonade.

00:06:47.890 --> 00:06:50.760
Is that island Sanshiroujima,
where the tombolo is?

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:52.280
Looks like it.

00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:54.680
I can't wait for the tombolo tomorrow.

00:06:54.910 --> 00:06:57.680
It's going to taste like pork jowl, right?

00:06:58.160 --> 00:06:59.690
That's right.

00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:04.630
We'll see the tombolo around noon,
 and it's not far from the campsite,

00:07:04.630 --> 00:07:06.860
so we can stay up all night tonight!

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:08.670
I got plenty of sleep on the way.

00:07:08.670 --> 00:07:10.790
I'm ready to stay up really late.

00:07:10.790 --> 00:07:11.660
What should we do?

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:13.200
What should we do tonight?!

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:16.950
Rin-chan's been pretty quiet.

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:21.210
She's been devoured by the hot spring.

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:26.460
She must be really tired after
 riding all the way from Minobu.

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:29.840
She's in the perfect condition 
for a bath, in a way.

00:07:30.020 --> 00:07:35.270
Rin-chan's experienced cold, 
sleepiness, and exhaustion.

00:07:36.050 --> 00:07:37.780
It's like <i>Moped's Journey</i>!

00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:44.690
This stuff's the best after a bath!

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:45.860
We have an old fart here.

00:07:47.190 --> 00:07:48.860
I know, right?!

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:58.740
<b>Nishiizu Replacement Driver Service</b>

00:07:55.220 --> 00:07:57.040
Thank you.

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:02.440
<i>Three Noguchi-sans...</i>

00:08:02.440 --> 00:08:07.630
<i></i>*If you drink, be sure to hire 
a taxi or a replacement driver

00:08:02.680 --> 00:08:07.630
<i>If you drink, be sure to hire 
a taxi or a replacement driver.</i>

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:10.730
Sorry we're so late.

00:08:10.730 --> 00:08:12.880
Not a problem.

00:08:13.320 --> 00:08:15.240
There are only two groups today.

00:08:15.240 --> 00:08:18.130
Feel free to camp wherever you like.

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:19.720
Thank you very much.

00:08:26.150 --> 00:08:28.940
We're still by the water!

00:08:32.630 --> 00:08:36.690
The sun's already set, so we 
should split up and start prepping.

00:08:36.690 --> 00:08:39.790
Aoi-chan and I will start making dinner.

00:08:39.940 --> 00:08:42.850
We'll set up the tent, then.

00:08:42.850 --> 00:08:43.790
Rin.

00:08:45.610 --> 00:08:47.490
She's already in sleep mode!

00:08:47.490 --> 00:08:49.040
Whoa, you're right!

00:08:49.540 --> 00:08:51.390
Rin-chan, are you going to sleep already?

00:08:51.390 --> 00:08:54.920
I'm about to make dinner
 with dried alfonsino.

00:08:54.920 --> 00:08:57.050
I know, I know...

00:08:57.690 --> 00:08:59.250
I know.

00:08:59.250 --> 00:09:00.710
Chill out.

00:09:01.210 --> 00:09:06.400
I'm just resting my eyes because I'm tired...

00:09:07.740 --> 00:09:08.940
Rin-chan!

00:09:09.120 --> 00:09:10.650
O-Oh, yeah! The campfire!

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:12.170
Let's make our campfire!

00:09:12.170 --> 00:09:13.750
I'll help!

00:09:21.390 --> 00:09:22.430
Now, then...

00:09:23.090 --> 00:09:24.450
We start with these.

00:09:24.850 --> 00:09:26.450
Pine cones?

00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:27.580
Hello

00:09:26.450 --> 00:09:27.580
Hello!

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:37.340
We use these as our fire starter 
and put smaller twigs on top first.

00:09:37.770 --> 00:09:40.720
Then we pile bigger logs on top.

00:09:46.380 --> 00:09:48.350
See? It was easy, right?

00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:52.090
I thought campfires were harder to make.

00:09:52.090 --> 00:09:54.860
Is this your first time making one?

00:09:56.510 --> 00:09:59.810
We made a bonfire with 
fallen leaves at school,

00:09:59.810 --> 00:10:02.120
but this is my first time doing it myself.

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:07.250
It's so warm, Rin-chan.

00:10:08.780 --> 00:10:10.270
Yeah...

00:10:13.770 --> 00:10:15.260
Aoi-chan!

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:18.880
Rin-chan has passed on.

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:30.210
<i>First, pour a cup of olive oil into a pot.</i>

00:10:30.210 --> 00:10:35.980
<i>Add minced garlic, chili peppers, 
and herb salt, and cook on low heat.</i>

00:10:37.190 --> 00:10:41.950
<i>When it gives off the tasty aroma 
of garlic, throw in some eggplant,</i>

00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:45.490
<i>champignons, shimeji mushrooms, 
and garlic, all chopped bite-sized.</i>

00:10:45.800 --> 00:10:47.460
<i>Bring to medium heat.</i>

00:10:48.210 --> 00:10:55.280
<i>When the eggplant is soft, add the octopus, 
shrimp, wieners, paprika, and young corn,</i>

00:10:55.280 --> 00:10:59.090
<i>as well as Chinese yams and broccoli 
that have been parboiled and strained.</i>

00:10:59.090 --> 00:11:01.260
<i>Continue cooking.</i>

00:11:01.440 --> 00:11:05.540
<i>Lastly, season with salt, pepper, and parsley,</i>

00:11:06.190 --> 00:11:07.830
<i>and you're done.</i>

00:11:07.430 --> 00:11:09.520
Chunky Ajillo in an Earthenware Pot

00:11:07.830 --> 00:11:09.520
Done!

00:11:09.780 --> 00:11:13.240
The garlic smells so good.

00:11:13.240 --> 00:11:15.510
It looks delicious.

00:11:15.510 --> 00:11:17.280
Smells yummy.

00:11:17.540 --> 00:11:20.280
Sensei, we're ready, too!

00:11:21.070 --> 00:11:23.780
Char-grilled Spiny Lobster

00:11:21.900 --> 00:11:23.780
May I?

00:11:23.970 --> 00:11:25.370
Go ahead.

00:11:25.370 --> 00:11:28.350
Oh, just please leave the shell.

00:11:28.350 --> 00:11:29.420
Okay.

00:11:29.420 --> 00:11:32.920
I feel bad having you girls 
do all this work, though.

00:11:33.250 --> 00:11:36.860
You were driving the whole day. 
You must be tired.

00:11:36.860 --> 00:11:39.150
We can handle some grilling.

00:11:39.150 --> 00:11:40.800
O-Okay.

00:11:41.830 --> 00:11:45.280
More like, if we let Sensei cook drunk...

00:11:45.280 --> 00:11:48.810
She would destroy the shell and 
make it unusable for the broth.

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:49.930
Local
Izu
Sake

00:11:57.070 --> 00:12:03.070
Arashibori

00:11:58.310 --> 00:12:00.240
That's the stuff!

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:03.070
Nothing pairs with spiny lobster
 better than sake.

00:12:03.410 --> 00:12:07.450
Good thing you had the right 
booze for our meal today, huh?

00:12:09.310 --> 00:12:11.200
I learned from my mistakes 
on our Christmas trip.

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:16.080
I brought plenty of liquors 
that pair with dinner!

00:12:16.080 --> 00:12:17.590
A-All of that?

00:12:20.920 --> 00:12:22.100
Ryouko?

00:12:22.360 --> 00:12:24.270
You're driving tomorrow, too.

00:12:24.270 --> 00:12:26.060
Don't let your evening drink get out of hand.

00:12:26.060 --> 00:12:27.470
Is she a mind reader?

00:12:28.890 --> 00:12:32.480
Well, it's a bit late, but...

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:34.040
Time for dinner.

00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:35.980
Let's eat.

00:12:39.150 --> 00:12:42.490
You can really taste the 
garlic in the young corn.

00:12:43.720 --> 00:12:46.240
The mushrooms and shrimp are good, too.

00:12:46.510 --> 00:12:49.500
<i>Whole garlic and Chinese yams...</i>

00:12:53.980 --> 00:12:55.830
<i>It's nice and hot.</i>

00:12:56.480 --> 00:13:00.550
<i>An umami and sleepiness double-whammy.</i>

00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:02.110
Rin-chan, are you all right?

00:13:02.820 --> 00:13:04.510
Hey, did you know?

00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:08.890
The "llo" in "ajillo" means 
to scream in Spanish.

00:13:09.400 --> 00:13:13.970
The word "ajillo" comes from how it's so 
good that it makes you scream "ajiii!"

00:13:13.970 --> 00:13:15.060
Sure, sure.

00:13:18.540 --> 00:13:20.270
Ajiii!

00:13:23.980 --> 00:13:29.030
Hey, Nadeshiko-chan, aren't we using the 
alfonsino we got from the dried goods store?

00:13:30.660 --> 00:13:32.560
Now, now, just be patient.

00:13:32.560 --> 00:13:34.290
We're just getting started.

00:13:35.020 --> 00:13:38.850
The juices from all the ingredients 
are mixed into the olive oil.

00:13:38.850 --> 00:13:40.170
Seems so.

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:42.850
You've got this, Nadeshiko-chan!

00:13:42.850 --> 00:13:44.420
Right!

00:13:46.240 --> 00:13:50.360
Add some more chili peppers, minced garlic, 
and veggies to the leftover olive oil,

00:13:50.360 --> 00:13:52.810
and turn on the heat.

00:13:53.130 --> 00:13:58.590
Once the veggies are cooked, 
we throw in the pre-grilled alfonsino.

00:13:59.440 --> 00:14:01.360
Here comes the alfonsino!

00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:03.690
We removed the head and bones.

00:14:04.030 --> 00:14:06.070
Set it to high heat.

00:14:06.520 --> 00:14:09.140
Add water and white wine.

00:14:09.140 --> 00:14:11.700
Ah, my white wine!

00:14:11.890 --> 00:14:14.830
Add some cherry tomatoes, 
and boil for a little longer.

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:18.710
Mix in some cooked pasta, 
sprinkle on black olives,

00:14:18.710 --> 00:14:23.090
capers, and basil, then give it 
some salt and pepper, and...

00:14:23.350 --> 00:14:27.040
We have alfonsino acqua pazza pasta!

00:14:27.040 --> 00:14:30.220
This is bound to be good!

00:14:34.600 --> 00:14:35.800
The umami of the alfonsino

00:14:35.800 --> 00:14:39.680
and the flavors of the ajillo ingredients
 are all over the pasta.

00:14:39.680 --> 00:14:41.850
This is way too good!

00:14:41.850 --> 00:14:43.110
Yum!

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:47.110
I char-grilled the heads, too. Try them out.

00:14:47.550 --> 00:14:50.170
I never knew you could eat 
the heads and bones, too.

00:14:50.170 --> 00:14:53.030
Someone at the shop told me.

00:14:54.300 --> 00:14:56.190
From ajillo to acqua pazza...

00:14:56.190 --> 00:14:58.250
A flowing reincarnation.

00:14:58.530 --> 00:15:00.480
Truly impeccable.

00:15:00.480 --> 00:15:03.000
You really raised the bar for tomorrow.

00:15:04.780 --> 00:15:07.540
You were doing research until 
just before we left, right?

00:15:07.540 --> 00:15:08.510
I was.

00:15:08.780 --> 00:15:11.480
Like about how this would be a good 
use of the oil from the ajillo,

00:15:11.480 --> 00:15:13.570
and how it makes clean-up easier.

00:15:13.570 --> 00:15:16.130
And how you don't need as much salt,

00:15:16.130 --> 00:15:19.270
because dried fish is 
saltier than regular fish.

00:15:19.270 --> 00:15:20.640
Wow.

00:15:21.010 --> 00:15:22.900
Nadeshiko-chan, Nadeshiko-chan!

00:15:23.260 --> 00:15:25.770
Rin-chan's departed.

00:15:29.520 --> 00:15:30.650
Come on, now.

00:15:30.650 --> 00:15:33.040
You have to brush your teeth before bed.

00:15:34.380 --> 00:15:36.270
Don't you need to put on lotion?

00:15:37.800 --> 00:15:38.810
I do...

00:15:38.810 --> 00:15:40.660
You should.

00:15:39.560 --> 00:15:40.660
Is she her mom?

00:15:40.660 --> 00:15:41.760
She's her mom.

00:15:41.760 --> 00:15:43.170
Mamashiko.

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:45.590
Thank you for the meal!

00:15:45.590 --> 00:15:48.920
Well, why don't we split up the work
 and get this all cleaned up?

00:15:50.060 --> 00:15:52.430
Hey, what are we doing next?

00:15:53.940 --> 00:15:56.290
We're going to watch all kinds of videos.

00:15:56.290 --> 00:15:58.320
What should we watch today?

00:15:58.320 --> 00:16:01.810
Oh, I wanna watch <i>A Zombie's Life</i>!

00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:03.810
Zombies?!

00:16:03.810 --> 00:16:06.940
A Zombie's Life

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:05.690
What's wrong, Nadeshiko-chan?

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:06.940
Can't handle scary movies?

00:16:07.160 --> 00:16:09.370
O-O-Of course I can!

00:16:09.370 --> 00:16:11.290
I'm totally good!

00:16:11.290 --> 00:16:13.180
Okay, let's watch this, then.

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:29.210
Ajiii!

00:16:45.240 --> 00:16:47.100
I can't fall asleep.

00:16:51.090 --> 00:16:51.610
Huh?

00:16:51.960 --> 00:16:53.330
Nadeshiko-chan?

00:16:53.330 --> 00:16:54.880
Oh, Ena-chan.

00:16:55.110 --> 00:16:57.990
Midnight Tea

00:16:56.120 --> 00:16:59.700
I can't sleep since I slept in the van.

00:17:00.630 --> 00:17:02.120
I thought so.

00:17:02.280 --> 00:17:03.680
Also...

00:17:03.680 --> 00:17:05.550
Zombies!

00:17:05.550 --> 00:17:07.630
Sheesh, you shouldn't have acted tough.

00:17:09.730 --> 00:17:11.760
This is such a nice campsite.

00:17:11.760 --> 00:17:13.340
Isn't it?

00:17:13.960 --> 00:17:18.240
I bet it gets really busy 
with beachgoers in summer.

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:20.390
I bet.

00:17:26.970 --> 00:17:33.400
I've always lived by the sea, 
so the sound of waves relaxes me.

00:17:34.240 --> 00:17:36.560
By the way, Ena-chan,

00:17:36.560 --> 00:17:39.560
you're working at the convenience 
store by my place, aren't you?

00:17:39.560 --> 00:17:41.580
I'm finally busted, huh?

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:43.910
I felt like a spy. It was kind of fun.

00:17:44.360 --> 00:17:47.560
Camping costs money, after all.

00:17:47.560 --> 00:17:48.690
Yeah.

00:17:48.690 --> 00:17:50.460
That, too, but...

00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:54.920
Ever since I started camping with everyone,

00:17:55.310 --> 00:17:59.380
I've been thinking I'd like to get my 
driver's license when I turn eighteen.

00:17:59.380 --> 00:18:00.300
Your license?

00:18:00.690 --> 00:18:04.540
You can only go so many places with your dog

00:18:04.540 --> 00:18:06.040
by bike or train.

00:18:06.730 --> 00:18:08.680
So I want to get my driver's license

00:18:09.060 --> 00:18:11.980
and take Chikuwa to all kinds of places.

00:18:13.130 --> 00:18:14.280
Yeah?

00:18:15.540 --> 00:18:17.840
Chikuwa's a lucky dog.

00:18:17.840 --> 00:18:20.240
It's really just that I want
 to take him places.

00:18:23.510 --> 00:18:29.210
I feel like a lot's changed 
since you moved here.

00:18:30.890 --> 00:18:31.910
Me, too.

00:18:32.610 --> 00:18:35.590
I think a lot's changed for me
 since I met you guys.

00:18:48.380 --> 00:18:50.970
I think I'm getting sleepy.

00:18:50.970 --> 00:18:52.480
Shall we head back?

00:18:52.740 --> 00:18:54.320
It's half past three.

00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:56.730
We stayed up pretty late.

00:18:57.660 --> 00:18:59.020
Goodnight.

00:18:59.020 --> 00:19:01.030
See you tomorrow, Ena-chan.

00:19:01.030 --> 00:19:02.350
Night.

00:19:16.210 --> 00:19:17.550
I slept well.

00:19:20.360 --> 00:19:21.870
<i>She's sound asleep.</i>

00:19:31.910 --> 00:19:33.550
I woke up too early.

00:19:35.150 --> 00:19:38.150
<b>Cape Kogane</b>

00:19:38.150 --> 00:19:45.660
Cape Kogane

00:19:38.490 --> 00:19:41.670
<i>Geospot number six: Cape Kogane.</i>

00:19:42.130 --> 00:19:45.660
<i>A cape in Nishiizu that is said to 
have the best sunset in Japan.</i>

00:19:47.040 --> 00:19:52.540
Horse Rocks

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:52.540
<i>The name comes from the way the 
whole cliff turns gold in the sunset.</i>

00:19:57.200 --> 00:19:58.310
<i>Guess I'll go back.</i>

00:20:08.670 --> 00:20:10.720
<i>I guess I'll take a look around.</i>

00:20:18.940 --> 00:20:20.940
<b>Sawada Park</b>

00:20:20.940 --> 00:20:29.370
Sawada Park

00:20:21.600 --> 00:20:25.120
<i>Geospot number seven: Sawada Park.</i>

00:20:25.770 --> 00:20:30.640
<i>The whole area is covered in a layer of 
volcanic ash from underwater volcanoes.</i>

00:20:30.640 --> 00:20:33.440
<i>There is an outdoor bath on the cliff.</i>

00:20:38.840 --> 00:20:42.160
I woke up too early, 
so I'm gonna go bike around.

00:20:42.160 --> 00:20:46.320
Aw, Rin-chan left by herself.

00:20:46.320 --> 00:20:48.170
She really did.

00:20:52.190 --> 00:20:55.390
I'm going to get some more 
sleep until Rin gets back.

00:20:59.250 --> 00:21:00.950
Me, too.

00:21:02.120 --> 00:21:04.360
Ena-chan, close the front for me.

00:21:04.360 --> 00:21:06.920
You do it, Aoi-chan.

00:21:09.030 --> 00:21:11.380
Guys! Get up! Bad news!

00:21:11.380 --> 00:21:13.060
Rin... Rin has..

00:21:12.450 --> 00:21:15.500
Please don't come looking for me.

00:21:13.470 --> 00:21:15.500
She's left home!

00:21:18.420 --> 00:21:20.000
So she did.

00:21:23.940 --> 00:21:25.750
A hot spring all to myself...

00:21:26.870 --> 00:21:29.020
Feels too good.

00:23:00.980 --> 00:23:03.480
<b>Inu Inu Inuko-san</b>

00:23:01.690 --> 00:23:03.480
Inu Inu Inuko-san!

00:23:03.480 --> 00:23:06.980
<b>Tengusa</b>

00:23:04.180 --> 00:23:09.740
<i>We made tokoroten using
 tengusa seaweed from Izu.</i>

00:23:12.410 --> 00:23:14.740
Something funny-looking's coming out.

00:23:14.970 --> 00:23:17.340
It's Mt. Fuji-shaped tokoroten!

00:23:17.340 --> 00:23:19.120
Cute, right?

00:23:27.360 --> 00:23:34.910
Next Episode

00:23:27.360 --> 00:23:34.910
<b>Izu Camping!!! Birthdays!</b>

00:23:34.370 --> 00:23:41.260
When camping...

00:23:34.370 --> 00:23:41.260
Always mind the campsite 
and facility rules. Don't forget to 
take care of fires and your trash!

00:23:34.370 --> 00:23:41.260
It gets cold during the winter. 
Stay warm and be well-prepared!

00:23:34.370 --> 00:23:41.260
Outdoor Activities Club

00:23:34.370 --> 00:23:41.260
Sleep, little one
